  "date": "October 2026",
  "abstract": "Covers OAuth 2.0 (RFC 6749, RFC 6750) as tightened by the RFC 9700 Security BCP, the RFC 10017 browser-based apps BCP and the RFC 10027 cross-device flows BCP and the OAuth 2.1 draft (-16, build posture), with the extensions a resource server, client or authorization server needs: PKCE, DPoP, mTLS-bound tokens, Rich Authorization Requests, token exchange, resource indicators, AS and protected resource metadata, the iss parameter, step-up, dynamic client registration, introspection, revocation and the device grant. Drafts for Client ID Metadata Documents, identity chaining, rfc7523bis, attestation-based client authentication, first-party apps, transaction tokens, RAR remediation, the Security BCP update, refresh token expiration, SPIFFE client authentication and deferred token responses are pinned with a posture. Version lines: OAuth 2.0 is current, OAuth 2.1 is a build-posture preview with a 2.0 to 2.1 upgrade checklist, and OAuth 1.0 (RFC 5849) is legacy, replaced rather than upgraded. SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references split out the version lines, the resource server, sender constraint, clients, the authorization server, delegation and drafts.",
